###############################################################################
# Q10 -- Benchmark results
###############################################################################

# No energy/force/stress accuracy metric is reported in a form the schema captures (see Q12).

###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Table S11 gives the cost in seconds per MD step for 432, 2000, 5488 and
# 11664 Mo atoms (LAMMPS, one core of an Intel i7-6850k 3.6 GHz); recorded as
# inferenceHardware on the five Mo models and as inferenceComplexity on the
# methods. No per-atom time is stated as such and no training cost is given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The energy and force MAEs of all 30 models (Figure 3) and the Delta-EOS values (Figure 5a) are given only as figures; no value is printed in the text, so no AccuracyMetric is encoded. The repository cited by the paper (mlearn) may carry the numbers.
# - Table II (lattice parameter, elastic constants, bulk modulus, vacancy formation and migration energies per model) has no MetricProperty in schema 0.1.2 and is not encoded.
# - Cutoff radii follow main-text Table I. The SI disagrees in places: Table S7 lists GAP cutoffs of 4.1 (Cu) and 5.1 (Si) against 3.9 and 5.4 in Table I, and the first page of Table S8 lists SNAP cutoffs of 3.8 (Cu), 5.2 (Mo), 5.0 (Ge) against 4.1, 4.6, 5.5 in Table I and on its own continuation pages.
# - Data set sizes per element are not stated in the text (only the 90:10 split and, for Mo, 'about 100 training structures' for the optimal models and up to about 800 in the convergence study).
# - The '# of polynomial powers' of Table S10 is encoded as mlips:momentLevel. Jmax for linear SNAP is not tabulated (Table S8 lists coefficients only); for qSNAP the Table S9 value is encoded as stated, without deciding whether it denotes J or 2J.
# - NNP hidden-layer sizes and GAP kernel counts appear only as figure annotations and are not encoded. The software used for the NNP and MTP fits is not named; SNAP/qSNAP and all timings ran in LAMMPS.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
